{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-14655",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The following triangle illustrates the information given.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266767/assets/0df6765fdd30cf0ac74268a4341309a593dd8019c7f66057d36bd4f6c4be5eb2.png)\n\nThe Law of Sines states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡X}=\\frac{y}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡Y}=\\frac{z}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡Z}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\nm∠X={43}^{∘},\\,m∠Y={56}^{∘},\\,y=9,\n$$\n\nand consequently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{43}^{∘}}=\\frac{9}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{56}^{∘}}.\n$$\n\nTo solve for $x,$ we multiply both sides by $\\operatorname{sin}⁡{43}^{∘}$ to give\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{43}^{∘}\\times \\frac{x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{43}^{∘}} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡{43}^{∘}\\times \\frac{9}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{56}^{∘}} \\\\ \\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{43}^{∘}}\\times \\frac{x}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{43}^{∘}}} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡{43}^{∘}\\times \\frac{9}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{56}^{∘}} \\\\ x & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡{43}^{∘}\\times \\frac{9}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{56}^{∘}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $\\operatorname{sin}⁡{43}^{∘}≈0.682$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡{56}^{∘}≈0.829,$ both rounded to four decimal places to avoid rounding error. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡{43}^{∘}\\times \\frac{9}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{56}^{∘}} \\\\  & ≈0.682\\times \\frac{9}{0.829} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{0.682\\times 9}{0.829} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{6.138}{0.829} \\\\  & ≈7.4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place.",
